<title>POLAND: Polish privatisation certificates expire end-98.</title>
<headline>Polish privatisation certificates expire end-98.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish mass privatisation certificates (PSU), which some 25.7 million adult Poles bought last year, will expire on December 31, 1998, the government's economic committee said in a statement late on Monday.</p>
<p>Before that date the certificates can be exchanged for 15 shares, one share in each of the country's 15 National Investment Funds (NFI) which run more than 500 companies that took part in the mass privatisation programme.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
